description:
This issue originates from Siroforce Ticket 8001318473. The root cause is not fully clear. However, within the logs we can see that the read of the calibration file fails:
{code:java}
2025-11-13 08:35:37,065 Velocity.VelocityHost.VelocityUsbDevice                      [59] ERROR - SendMessageAndReadResponse (961) - An error occurred reading payload. Total bytes received: 0, NtStatus: 0x000003E3, UsbdStatus: 0xC0010000{code}
This results in the sensor never becoming exposure ready, because the calibration file is not available due to the failed read.
{code:java}
Velocity.VelocityDevice.VelocityDevice                       [32] WARN  - Attempted to enabled exposure without Calibration data {code}
The proposed fix is to retry reading the calibration file when the read fails or when the calibration file is corrupted. Or save the calib file in general for a sensor on the hard drive.

h2. Summary

When the SSE (Server-Sent Events) connection between the Sidexis Acquisition App and the IO-Sensor-Service is interrupted, the InUse lock on the device is not released. Subsequent acquisition sessions cannot claim the sensor - it remains in status "InUse" and is displayed as "not available".
h2. Steps to Reproduce
 # Sensor/USB box is connected and recognized
 # First acquisition session is started -> device changes to "InUse"
 # SSE connection is lost (e.g. due to timeout, network issue, or Sidexis navigates away)
 # New acquisition session is opened for a different patient
 # Sensor is visible in the device list but marked as "not available" (Status: InUse from previous session)
 # User unplugs and reconnects USB box -> sensor is briefly recognized but InUse lock blocks access again

h2. Expected Result

When the SSE connection drops or a session is not cleanly terminated, the IO-Sensor-Service should automatically release the InUse lock after a timeout, making the sensor available for new sessions.
h2. Actual Result

The InUse lock persists indefinitely. The sensor is blocked for all subsequent sessions until the service is restarted.
h2. Environment
 * *Siroforce Ticket:* 8001405336
 * *Logs:* H:\GBE\Extern\Exchange\Austausch_BackOffice\8001405336
 * *Date of incident:* 2026-02-17, approx. 14:31 - 15:20
 * *Video:* VIDEO-2026-02-17-15-20-46.mp4 (shows user unplugging and reconnecting USB box)

h2. Log Analysis (2026-02-17)
 * 14:31:26 - First acquisition session (Order 8153e0c1) created, device changes to InUse
 * 14:33:22 - Second acquisition session (Order 5fecc0dc) started, RemoteLogger reports "Last Used device not available" and "State: NoHardware"
 * 14:35:46 - Cleanup function triggered, finds open session, but device remains InUse
 * 15:08:02 - Third acquisition session started, again "NoHardware" and "Last Used device not available"
 * 15:08:25 - User physically unplugs USB box (SafeXferData detected device unplugged)
 * 15:08:28 - USB box is recognized again, but InUse lock prevents access

h2. Root Cause (confirmed in code)
When the SSE connection drops, the {{ClientHeartbeatMonitor}} detects it (exception on heartbeat send) and calls {{client.CloseStream()}}. Similarly, {{SendStatusEvent()}} catches the exception and calls {{UnsubscribeFromStatusEvents()}}. However, *neither of these paths calls EndSession()*. The client is removed from the SSE subscription list, but the {{AcquisitionSession}} itself stays alive in the {{AcquisitionManager._acquisitionSessions}} dictionary with the device still locked as {{DeviceStatus.InUse}}.

The only way the InUse lock is released is through {{AcquisitionSession.EndSession()}} (line 240: {{Device.DeviceStatus = DeviceStatus.Available}}), which is only called when the client explicitly sends a DELETE request to {{/api/dsio/modality/v1/acquisition/\{sessionId\}}}.

*Relevant code:*
* {{ClientHeartbeatMonitor.cs:72-76}} - detects dead connection, only closes stream
* {{AcquisitionSession.cs:1231-1236}} - detects dead client in SendStatusEvent, only unsubscribes
* {{AcquisitionSession.cs:218-268}} - EndSession() which actually releases the InUse lock - never called on SSE disconnect
* {{AcquisitionManager.cs:190-201}} - EndSession() entry point - only triggered by explicit DELETE request

h2. Proposed Fix
Add orphan session detection to the {{AcquisitionSession}}. When the last SSE client disconnects (i.e. {{_connectedClients}} becomes empty), start a configurable timeout (e.g. 30 seconds). If no client reconnects within that window, automatically call {{AcquisitionManager.EndSession()}} to release the InUse lock and clean up the session.

Implementation approach:
{code:csharp}
// In AcquisitionSession.UnsubscribeFromStatusEvents():
public void UnsubscribeFromStatusEvents(ClientSubscription<AcquisitionStatus> client)
{
    Log.Info("Removing client from Acquisition Status subscription");
    if (_connectedClients.TryRemove(client, out var clientMonitor))
    {
        clientMonitor.StopHeartbeatMonitor();
        client.CloseStream();
        Log.Debug("Client removed from Acquisition Status subscription");

        // If no more clients are connected, start orphan timeout
        if (_connectedClients.IsEmpty)
        {
            Log.Warn("All SSE clients disconnected. Starting orphan session timeout.");
            StartOrphanSessionTimeout();
        }
    }
}

private CancellationTokenSource _orphanTimeoutCts;
private void StartOrphanSessionTimeout()
{
    _orphanTimeoutCts?.Cancel();
    _orphanTimeoutCts = new CancellationTokenSource();
    var token = _orphanTimeoutCts.Token;

    Task.Delay(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(30), token).ContinueWith(t =>
    {
        if (!t.IsCanceled && _connectedClients.IsEmpty)
        {
            Log.Warn($"Orphan session timeout reached for session {SessionId}. No clients reconnected. Requesting session cleanup.");
            OnOrphanSessionDetected?.Invoke(SessionId);
        }
    });
}

// Cancel timeout if a new client subscribes
public void SubscribeToStatusEvents(ClientSubscription<AcquisitionStatus> client)
{
    _orphanTimeoutCts?.Cancel(); // Cancel orphan timeout
    // ... existing code ...
}
{code}

The {{AcquisitionManager}} would subscribe to {{OnOrphanSessionDetected}} and call {{EndSession()}} to release the device.

h2. Workaround
Restart the IO-Sensor-Service to clear all orphaned InUse locks. After restart, the sensor will be available for new acquisition sessions again.

Note: Restarting Sidexis alone does not help, as the orphaned session is held server-side in the IO-Sensor-Service, not in Sidexis.

h2. Related Issues
* [S4SP-345|https://jira.dentsplysirona.com/browse/S4SP-345] - Device is still "In Use" if Sidexis crashes (same effect, was only fixed for crash scenario)
* [S4SP-1035|https://jira.dentsplysirona.com/browse/S4SP-1035] - Exposure readiness takes up to 10 minutes (similar symptoms)
